            0.214,
            0.201,
            0.785,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The goal is C ∧ D. What solution is returned by POP? What solution is returned by GraphPlan? (If there are multiple answers, give them.) What does this example reveal about the expressive power of the solution descriptions in the two algorithms?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.284,
            0.458,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8 More GraphPlan"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.316,
            0.785,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It has been suggested that the first phase of GraphPlan be used as a heuristic function for forward search in the following way: Given a state s and goal g, run the graph-construction phases of GraphPlan until all the components are present and not mutex in the last layer. Let n be the number of action layers in the graph. We will let n be the heuristic value for s. Is this an admissible heuristic?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.429,
            0.481,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9 Bayesian Networks"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.46,
            0.382,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider this network:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.478,
            0.311,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.215,
                0.478,
                0.311,
                0.623
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.626,
            0.755,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Which of the following conditional independence assumptions are true?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.654,
            0.446,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. A and E are independent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.234,
            0.679,
            0.506,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. A and E are independent given D."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.234,
            0.705,
            0.446,
            0.72
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. B and C are independent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.234,
            0.729,
            0.506,
            0.745
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. B and C are independent given A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.755,
            0.506,
            0.77
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. B and C are independent given D."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.234,
            0.78,
            0.506,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. A and E are independent given B."
            }
          ]
        },
